==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|Wage||archaic since 1927; nonstandard since 1996}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|wāge}}, from {{inh|de|goh|wāga}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*wēgō|t=scales}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|waag}}, {{m+|en|wey}}.

The spelling {{m|de||Waage}} was used alongside {{m|de|Wage}} since at least the 17th century. As the etymological school of the 19th century favoured single vowels, some doubled spellings like {{m|de|baar}}, {{m|de|Schooß}}, {{m|de||Waage}} were abolished during the {{w|German_Orthographic_Conference_of_1901|reforms of the early 20th century}}. However, the spelling {{m|de||Waage}} was standardised again by two decrees from the governments of Austria (March 1927) and Germany (July 1927) in order to avoid the ambiguity between plural {{m|de|Waagen}} and {{m|de|Wagen|t=car[s], carriage[s]}}, as for example in {{m|de|Waagenbau|t=construction of scales}} versus {{m|de|Wagenbau|t=construction of cars}}.<ref>[http://www.rechtschreib-werkstatt.de/GrafOrtho/woerter/w-w/html/waage-erlass.html Erlass des Reichsministers des Innern vom 05. Juli 1927], at www.rechtschreib-werkstatt.de</ref>

